- The two QNEthernet copies are the same fork and are meant to stay
  byte-identical; both carry the multicast TTL and DSCP additions that the
  AES67 sender and the PTP transport call. They report the same version
  string, and that string is only honest while they match.
- `packages/t41-ptp/libraries/Time` says in every source file that the reader
  "should have received a copy of the GNU Lesser General Public License", and
  upstream ships none. The `COPYING` in that directory is the licence text
  from gnu.org, added here so the copy exists.
- Combining GPL-3.0 code with the MIT and BSD components above is what those
  licences allow; their notices are retained. The LGPL-2.1 component is used
  as a library and is not modified here.
